          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "боль (bol) — \"pain\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "боль (bol) from Proto-Slavic bolĭ — inherited, with the verb болеть, \"to ache, to be ill\". Vasmer sets it beside Gothic balwjan, \"to torment\", and Old English bealu, \"evil\", the bale of baleful, but notes that Berneker rejected the link."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
