          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "лекарство (lekárstvo) is лекарь, an old word for \"doctor\", with the noun suffix -ство. The root лек-, \"cure\", came into Slavic from Germanic; Vasmer calls the loan certain and compares Gothic lēkeis, \"doctor\". English leech, an old word for \"physician\", is from that Germanic word."
            }
          ]
        },
