        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "врач (vrach) — a Church Slavonic word, Old Church Slavonic vračĭ; its -ра-, where East Slavic would say -оро-, marks it. Vasmer derives it from the root of врать, \"to talk nonsense\", and ворчать, \"to grumble\", so the first sense was \"charmer, healer by spells\"; Bulgarian врач (vrach) still means \"sorcerer\"."
            }
          ]
        },
